<CustomMetadata
  xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
>
    <label>Apex - SOQL or DML inside a loop</label>
    <protected>true</protected>
    <values>
        <field>Domain__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">ApexClass</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>IsEnabled__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:boolean">true</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>Severity__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">High</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>Category__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">Performance</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>Confidence__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">Low</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>Threshold__c</field>
        <value xsi:nil="true" />
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>Description__c</field>
        <value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >A SOQL query or a DML statement appears inside the body of a for, while or do loop.</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>Rationale__c</field>
        <value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >Queries and DML inside loops consume governor limits per iteration and fail on bulk operations (data loads, integrations, mass updates). Detection is a static heuristic: the loop may be bounded in practice, so confirm by reading the code.</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>SuggestedAction__c</field>
        <value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >Collect the records first, run one query or one DML on the whole collection outside the loop, and use maps for lookups.</value>
    </values>
</CustomMetadata>
